# Ray Tracer Project

## Overview
This project is a ray tracer implementation built from scratch.

## The Journey
Building a ray tracer from the ground up is no joke I almost had a sesuire. There were plenty of moments where I hit my keyboard trying to get the math right, optimize performanc, and debug rendering issues. But honestly, the experience was shiting. Having access to good documentation made a huge difference—it helped me understand the concepts better and produce soemthing.

## Key learnings
- Understanding ray-object intersection calculations
- implementing lighting and shading models
- optimizing for performance
- Debugging visual artifacts

## Results
You can check out some of the rendered images and results in the GitHub repo. Ive stored a few examples showing different scenes and features the tracer can handle.

## How to Use
The project is fairly straight to run. Just follow the setup instructions and you should be good to go.

## Conclusion
This was a fun project that really disturebed my understanding of computer graphics. If you're interested in ray tracing, feel free to explore the code and the results